Task: Fix the false "fit N/8, below 5" reason in the HTML report's "Close but excluded" list
Action: Root cause: state.rank sets show = eligible and shown < result_count, but report._excluded_reason only knew "gate failed" and "below 5", so an eligible row cut by the count (and a fit-5+ row with an unanswered gate) read "below 5". _excluded_reason now takes the shown count and returns "fit N/8, not in the top R" for eligible rows, "not all gates checked" for a fit-5+ row with a missing gate, and "below 5" only under 5. Reasons are set after the loop, once the shown count is known. New test failed first (reproduced), then passed.
